            %p The interpretation of the stages is as indicated in the diagram:
            %ol
              %li
                %p the top morphism is the transition function of the underlying bundle;
              %li
                %p the middle morphism is a choice of (pseudo-)connection on that bundle;
              %li
                %p the bottom morphism picks up the curvature of this connection.
            %p
              We will see that full
              = succeed "-Chern-Weil" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphism"} connecting homomorphism
              %em curvature
              is exhibited as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} obstruction cocycle
              to lifts from bare bundles to flat bundles.
          .num_remark
            %h6#observation_7 Observation
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} C(U) \stackrel{g}{\to} \mathbf{B}U(1)
              the cocycle for a
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
