                  }
          %p together with a constraint on the bottom morphism.
          %p
            It is in the form of such a kind of diagram that the general notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} connections on ∞-bundles
            may be modeled. In the full theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
            this follows from first principles, but for our present introductory purpose we shall be content with taking this simple situation of
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            as sufficient motivation for the constructions considered now.
          %p
            So we pass now to what is to some extent the reverse construction of the one considered before: we define a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+differential+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued differential forms
            and show how by a variant of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            these integrate to coefficient objects for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} connections on ∞-bundles
          %p
            In the main entry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory
            we discuss how this dg-algebraic construction follows from a general abstract definitions of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p
            The material of this section is due to (
            %a{:href => "#SSSI"}> SSSI
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#FSS"}> FSS
            ).
          %h4#CurvCharAndCS Curvature characteristics and Chern-Simons forms
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a Lie group, we have described
            %a{:href => "#ConnectionOnPrincipalBundle"} above
            connections on
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie-algebra+valued+forms"} groupoid of Lie-algebra valued forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mi conn
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi connection
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mo ∇
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mi diff
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi pseudo
                          %mo −
                          %mi connection
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∇
                                  %mi ps
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mo ≃
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi transition
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi function
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mo ≃
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}G_{conn} &amp;&amp;&amp; connection
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\nabla}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}G_{diff} &amp;&amp;&amp; pseudo-connection
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\nabla_{ps}}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                  \\\
                  C(U) &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}G &amp;&amp;&amp; transition\;function
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                  \\\
                  X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            In this context we had
            %em derived
            Lie algebra valued forms from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            description
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi conn
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi P
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn} = [\mathbf{P}_1(-), \mathbf{B}G]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            to construct parallel transport from Lie-algebra valued forms. The construction is such that it generalizes verbatim to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued forms
          %p
            For that purpose notice that another classical dg-algebra associated with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g})
          .num_lemma
            %h6#fact Fact
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{W}(\mathfrak{g})
              is the free dg-algebra on the graded vector space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} dgAlg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Vect
                          %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathrm{dgAlg}}(W(\mathfrak{g}), A) \simeq \mathrm{Hom}_{\mathrm{Vect}_{\mathbb{Z}}}(\mathfrak{g}^*, A)
                    \\,,
            %p
              which is singled out among the isomorphism class of dg-algebras with this property by the fact that the projection of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^* \oplus \mathfrak{g}^*[1] \to \mathfrak{g}^*
              extends to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ←
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(\mathfrak{g}) \leftarrow W(\mathfrak{g}) : i^*
                    \\,.
          %p
            (Notice that general the dg-algebras that we are dealing with are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-free+dga"} semi-free dga
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
            is free, but not the differential).
          %p
            The most obvious realization of the free dg-algebra on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet (\mathfrak{g}^* \oplus \mathfrak{g}^*[1])
            equipped with the differential that is precisely the degree shift isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : \mathfrak{g}^* \to \mathfrak{g}^*[1]
            extended as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet (\mathfrak{g}^* \oplus \mathfrak{g}^*[1])
            is given on the unshifted generators by the sum of the CE-differential with the shift isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi σ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{W(\mathfrak{g})}|_{\mathfrak{g}^*} = d_{CE(\mathfrak{g})} + \sigma
                  \\,.
          %p
            This uniquely fixes the differential on the shifted generators – a phenomenon known (at least after mapping this to differential forms, as we discuss below) as the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identity"} Bianchi identity
          %p
            Using this, we can express also the presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
            from def
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BGdiff"}
            in diagrammatic fashion.
          .num_lemma
            %h6#observation_9 Observation
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected"} simply connected
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{diff} \in [CartSp^{op}, Grpd]
              is isomorphic to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi diff
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↦
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi Ω
                                  %mi vert
                                  %mo •
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi U
                                %mo ×
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi k
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ←
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi A
                                      %mi vert
                              %mtd
                                %mi CE
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mi Ω
                                  %mo •
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi U
                                %mo ×
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi k
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ←
                                  %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mi W
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo }
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B}G_{diff}  =
                    \\tau_1
                    \\left(
                    \\exp(\mathfrak{g})_{diff}
                    \:
                    (U,[k]) \mapsto
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\Omega^\bullet_{vert}(U \times \Delta^k)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{A_{vert}}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    CE(\mathfrak{g})
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                    \\\
                    \\Omega^\bullet(U \times \Delta^k)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{A}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    W(\mathfrak{g})
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\right)
                    \\,
            %p where on the right we have the 1-truncation of the simplicial presheaf of diagrams as indicated, where the vertical morphisms are the canonical ones.
          %p
            Here over a given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            the bottom morphism in such a diagram is an arbitrary
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times \Delta^k
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi U
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi vert
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = A_U + A_{vert}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_U
            vanishes on tangents to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^k
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi vert
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{vert}
            on tangents to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi vert
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{vert}
            has to be such that the curvature 2-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi vert
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{A_{vert}}
            vanishes when both its arguments are tangent to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^k
          %p
            On the other hand, there is in the above no further constraint on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\mathfrak{g})_{diff}
            we find that morphisms are of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_U)_1 \stackrel{g}{\to} (A_U)_2
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi U
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_U)^i
            arbitrary. This is the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_10 Remark
            %p
              We see below that it is not a coincidence that this is reminiscent to the first condition on an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connection"} Ehresmann connection
              on a
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
              may be thought of as the
              = succeed "-sheaf" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %em trivial
              = succeed "-bundles." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We now want to lift the
            %a{:href => "#LieIntOfCocycles"} above
            construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\mu)
            of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-groupoid#IntegrationOfCocycles"} Lie integration of Lie algebra cocycles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            from plain bundles classified by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            to bundles with (pseudo-)connection classified by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{diff}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\mu)
            from a map on just
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\mathfrak{g})
            to a map on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\mathfrak{g})_{diff}
          %p
            This is evidently achieved by completing a square in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgAlg"} dgAlg
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi CE
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mi μ
                        %mtd
                          %mi CE
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mi cs
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  CE(\mathfrak{g}) &amp;\stackrel{\mu}{\leftarrow}&amp; CE(b^{n-1} \mathbb{R})
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                  \\\
                  W(\mathfrak{g}) &amp;\stackrel{cs}{\leftarrow}&amp; W(b^{n-1} \mathbb{R})
                  }
          %p
            and defining
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi diff
                  %mo :
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi diff
                  %mo →
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi ℝ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\mu)_{diff} : \exp(\mathfrak{g})_{diff} \to \exp(b^{n-1}\mathbb{R})_{diff}
            to be the operation of forming
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
            composites with this.
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(b^{n-1}\mathbb{R})
            is the Weil algebra of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie-algebra"} Lie n-algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b^{n-1} \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            with the differential given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi b
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi c
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{W(b^{n-1} \mathbb{R})} : c \mapsto k
          %p
            The commutativity of this diagram says that the bottom morphism takes the degree-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            generator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            to an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cs
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs \in W(\mathfrak{g})
            whose restriction to the unshifted generators is the given cocycle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
            As we shall see below, any such choice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs
            will extend the characteristic cocycle obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\mu)
            to a characteristic differential cocycle, exhibiting the
            = succeed "-Chern-Weil" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs
            will this take genuine
            = succeed "-connections" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-connections" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-connection"} pseudo-connection
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory
            = succeed "-Chern-Weil" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-connections." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            This is achieved by imposing the following additional constraint on the choice of extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_17 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \in CE(\mathfrak{g})
              a cocycle and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cs
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs \in W(\mathfrak{g})
              a lift of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ←
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g}) \leftarrow CE(\mathfrak{g})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle \in W(\mathfrak{g})
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
              %em in transgression
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              if
            %ul
              %li
                both
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle
                as well as
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{W(\mathfrak{g})}\langle - \rangle
                sit entirely in the shifted generators, in that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo •
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in \wedge^\bullet \mathfrak{g}^*[1] \hookrightarrow W(\mathfrak{g})
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
          %p
            To see this explicitly, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{t^a\}
            be a basis of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{r^a\}
            the corresponding basis of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*[1]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{C^a{}_{b c}\}
            for the structure constants of the Lie bracket in this basis.
          %p
            Then for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi k
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi r
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P = P_{(a_1 , \cdots , a_k)} r^{a_1} \wedge \cdots \wedge r^{a_k} \in \wedge^{r} \mathfrak{g}^*[1]
            an element in the shifted generators, the condition that it is
            = succeed "-closed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{W(\mathfrak{g})}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                    %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C^{b}_{c (a_1} P_{b, \cdots, a_k)} t^c \wedge r^{a_1} \wedge \cdots \wedge r^{a_k}
                  \\,,
          %p where the parentheses around indices denotes symmetrization, as usual, so that this is equivalent to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi i
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi i
                    %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi b
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_{i} C^{b}_{c (a_i} P_{a_1 \cdots a_{i-1} b a_{i+1} \cdots, a_k)}
                  \= 0
          %p for all choices of indices. This is the component-version of the familiar invariance statement
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mi i
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_i P(t_1, \cdots, t_{i-1}, [t_c, t_i], t_{i+1}, \cdots , t_k)
                  \= 0
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_\bullet \in  \mathfrak{g}
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_18 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inv(\mathfrak{g}) \subset W(\mathfrak{g})
              (or
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi basic
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g})_{basic}
          .num_prop
            %h6#observation_10 Observation
            %p
              We have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi b
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi b
                        %mi n
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(b^{n-1}\mathbb{R}) \simeq CE(b^n \mathbb{R})
          %p
            Using this, we can now encode the two conditions on the extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs
            of the cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            as the commutativity of this double square diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi CE
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mi μ
                        %mtd
                          %mi CE
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi cocycle
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mi cs
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Chern
                          %mo −
                          %mi Simons
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi element
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi inv
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mi inv
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi invariant
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi polynomial
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  CE(\mathfrak{g}) &amp;\stackrel{\mu}{\leftarrow}&amp; CE(b^{n-1} \mathbb{R})
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp; cocycle
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                  \\\
                  W(\mathfrak{g}) &amp;\stackrel{cs}{\leftarrow}&amp; W(b^{n-1} \mathbb{R})
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp; Chern-Simons\;element
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow &amp;&amp; \uparrow
                  \\\
                  inv(\mathfrak{g})
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\langle -\rangle}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                  inv(b^{n-1} \mathbb{R})
                  \&amp;&amp;&amp;
                  invariant\;polynomial
                  }
                  \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_19 Definition
            %p
              In such a diagram, we call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cs
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs
              the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
              that exhibits the transgression between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle - \rangle
          %p
            We shall see below that under the
            = succeed "-Chern-Weil" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+form"} Chern-Simons form
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/secondary+characteristic+class"} secondary characteristic class
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
          .num_note
            %h6#observation_11 Observation
            %p
              What this diagram encodes is the construction of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphism"} connecting homomorphism
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} long exact sequence in cohomology
              that is induced from the short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ker(i^*) \to W(\mathfrak{g}) \to CE(\mathfrak{g})
            %p subject to the extra constraint of basic elements.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi d
                                    %mi W
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi μ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi cs
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi CE
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ←
                          %mtd
                            %mi inv
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
